{
  "text": "2002B01 Outline\nthe influences of pregnancy on pharmacokinetics.\nList:\n·\nAbsorption\n·\nDistribution\n·\nMetabolism\n·\nExcretion\nAbsorption:\nOral\n·\n↓Gastric emptying in labour -> ↑risk\n  aspiration\nInhaled\n·\n↑VA\n  (progesterone on respiratory centre), ↓FRC (diaphragm compression) ->\n  ↑rate of volatile wash-in\n·\n(partly\n  offset by ↑cardiac output)\nSC/IM\n·\n↑blood flow -> ↑absorption rate (e.g. IM\n  morphine in labour)\nDistribution:\nCardiac output\n·\n↑CO\n  due to ↑preload, ↓afterload, ↑heart rate\n·\n↑Rate\n  of onset suxamethonium\n·\n↑Rate\n  of offset by distribution of propofol -> risk of awareness\n·\nSlows\n  onset of volatile anaesthetic (but ↑V\nA\n:FRC ratio is more\n  significant)\nBlood\n·\n↓Albumin\n  -> ↑free acidic drug (e.g. barbiturate) (note same total amount albumin)\n·\n↓AAG\n  -> ↑free basic drug (e.g. morphine)\n·\nRespiratory\n  alkalosis -> ↑% unionized basic drugs, ↓%unionised acidic drug\n·\n↑Blood\n  volume -> ↑V\nD\nplasma-confined drugs e.g. heparins\nTissues\n·\n↑Muscle\n  mass, ↑fat mass, oedema, ↑body water\n·\nHence\n  ↑V\nD\nmost drugs -> ↑t\n1/2\nβ\nmost drugs\nMetabolism and\nexcretion:\nLiver\n·\nUnchanged\n  hepatic blood flow and liver function\n·\nProgesterone\n  -> CYP enzyme induction\n·\nOestrogen\n  -> CYP enzyme competition\n·\n↓[Plasma\n  cholinesterase] but unchanged amount\nKidney\n·\n↑Renal blood flow 80% -> ↑GFR ->\n  ↑excretion unchanged drugs e.g. LMWH\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
